&lt;p&gt;Scale AI&#39;s Employee Relations team partners across the business to resolve workplace issues fairly, consistently, and in a way that protects both our people and the company. As we scale headcount across the US and Mexico, we&#39;re looking for an Employee Relations Partner to independently own our North America caseload — from performance management through investigations and separations — working closely with Legal, HR Business Partners, and all Business Units. This role will report to the Senior Director, Employee Relations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role calls for a genuine problem solver: someone who can walk into a messy, ambiguous case with no exact precedent and quickly build a sound, seamless path forward on their own.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You will:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently manage a full caseload of ER cases across the US (and support Mexico as needed), including performance issues, investigations, and separations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose ambiguous, novel workplace issues and construct a clear path forward when there&#39;s no clean policy or precedent to lean on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct thorough, timely, and legally-sound workplace investigations from intake to closure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise and coach managers through sensitive performance and conduct conversations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner directly with Legal to assess risk and align on documentation and resolution strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clear, defensible case documentation in our case management system (HR Acuity).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage separations end-to-end, including coordination with Workplace and Legal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support HRBPs with ER training, policy guidance, and escalation triage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to scaling ER infrastructure, including our Whistleblower Hotline and Competitors Escalation Program.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ideally you&#39;d have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of employee relations experience, including direct ownership of workplace investigations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of solving genuinely ambiguous, first-of-their-kind cases — not just executing an existing playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of US employment law.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supported Global teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using a formal ER case management system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written communication and documentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment handling highly confidential and sensitive information.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting ER matters outside the US (Mexico a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience at a high-growth tech or startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience helping build or scale ER processes/infrastructure from an early stage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting employees in EMEA region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
